  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 5935,
  "title": "Give Fluent suggested actions a solid background in forced colors",
  "body": "> In Windows contrast themes, Fluent suggested actions are see-through: a host page background image shows behind their text.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed Fluent suggested actions showing the page background through them in forced colors, in PR [#5935](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5935), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nThe Fluent suggested action has `background: transparent`, and forced colors keep a transparent background transparent, so the button text sits on whatever the host page draws behind Web Chat. In forced colors, the suggested action now uses `ButtonFace` as its background, also when hovered or pressed; nothing changes without forced colors.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `fluent-theme/.../SuggestedAction.module.css`: `background-color: ButtonFace` in forced colors\n- `fluentTheme/suggestedActions.forcedColors.html` and `.dark.html` (new): snapshot 1, both suggested actions are solid over a striped host page background in light and dark forced colors\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n\n",
